references/bpc/NDV.md:142:**Consensus finding:** Dedicated sensory relief spaces improve self-regulation outcomes for NDV/AUT populations; individual occupant control of sensory inputs is the highest-confidence design variable, more important than static environmental parameters; location adjacent to primary circulation with transition zone and acoustic separation is confirmed best practice.
references/bpc/NDV.md:144:**Best-practice provision (confirmed or upgraded from existing A-16):**
