references/bpc/bathrooms-and-wet-areas/bathroom-typology-global-south.md:79:| **1. Open-plan wet room** | All five accessible principles transfer directly: threshold (zero-threshold with floor drain), surface (wet COF ≥0.5), space (1500mm turning), support (grab bars per existing BPC), controls (lever taps, accessible height). | Floor gradient specification: ≥1:50, ≤1:40 (wheelchair stability constraint on drainage slope). Material options expanded: unglazed ceramic, sealed concrete, non-slip vinyl (cost-appropriate alternatives to porcelain tile). | None — this typology IS the best-practice specification. |
